# infra/.gitignore — generated and machine-local Terraform artefacts.
# Repo-wide Terraform ignores (.terraform/, *.tfstate, crash logs) live in the root
# .gitignore; only the infra-specific ones belong here.

# providers.tf and versions.tf inside live/<stage>/ are GENERATED: stage.sh's
# sync_templates copies them from infra/_common/ on `make init`. Those two templates are
# the single source of truth — edit them and re-run `make init`, or
# `make init FLAGS=--force` to overwrite a copy that has drifted.
#
# 00-backend-bootstrap is exempt: it declares its own provider and required_providers
# inline in main.tf (chicken/egg — it creates the backend), so it is never synced and has
# no copy to ignore.
live/*/providers.tf
live/*/versions.tf

# Data dir for `make validate` / `stage.sh validate`. Deliberately NOT named .terraform,
# so that a credential-free validate cannot disturb the real `init`. That also means the
# root .gitignore's `**/.terraform/*` rule does not cover it — hence this entry.
live/*/.terraform-validate/

# Saved plan files, e.g. `terraform plan -out=tfplan`. These embed variable values and
# can contain secrets, so they must never be committed.
*.tfplan

# Left behind when an apply is interrupted while holding the state lock.
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
